{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "EmissionsColumn",
    "description": "WRF-Chem's emissions_driver for the EqAtmChem configuration (chem_opt = 170 CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP, emiss_opt = 4 ecbmz_mosaic, bio_emiss_opt = 1 GUNTHER1), assembled from its four schemes and exposed as COLUMN tendencies of the CBM-Z gases and of the MOSAIC section masses and numbers, the form a chemistry column adds to each species' other tendencies.\n\nMounted by reference, in emissions_driver's call order: Bio (GuntherBiogenicEmissions, bio_emissions), Anthro (CBMZAnthroEmissions, cbmz_addemiss_anthro), BioCbmz (GuntherToCBMZ, add_biogenics' GUNTHER1 branch) and Aer (MosaicAnthroEmissions, the anthropogenic part of mosaic_addemiss). The one edge between two schemes is e_bio, Bio -> BioCbmz. EmissionsColumn holds the column state the driver reads (T, p, rho, alt, ze over the column; gsw, land use, day, input variety, MOSAIC's section centre volumes) and hands each scheme the emission layer's values. The emitted fluxes themselves are the schemes' own parameters (Anthro.E_*, Aer.E_*), set per test: they are data, read from the wrfchemi stream, and no scheme shares one.\n\nEvery emission is an in-place increment proportional to dt with no rate hidden inside it, so the tendencies are exact, not operator-split approximations (wrf_emission_templates.esm). The anthropogenic and biogenic contributions to the same CBM-Z species are summed on the coupling edge that sets sfc_<species>; twelve species receive both. Each surface tendency is put in layer 1 and zero above, because kemit = 1 in this configuration and emissions_driver touches no other layer (asserted: every test checks the whole 59-layer column). A consumer that integrates the column adds d<species>_dt to that species' state; a surface FLUX boundary condition on the vertical mixing would be the continuous alternative, but WRF applies emissions as a source in the bottom layer, after and separately from vertmx, and this document reproduces that.\n\nWhat the tests pin. Each test is one step of the separate emissions capture (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_emis.sh; the reference chem170 run has no emissions), and its expected values are the WHOLE emissions_driver increment, (chem_out - chem_in)/dt, of a real64 replay that calls the four Fortran routines in the driver's order -- so unlike the component tests, which assert each stage on its own inputs, e_bio here is computed by Bio and reaches add_biogenics through the coupling. Every species that changes at a step is asserted (the fill script, tools/fill_emissions_column_tests.py, refuses a case where something changes that this document does not expose); 58 of the 233 species change at a daytime step. Mutation checks: removing the e_bio edge fails 48 assertions, dropping the biogenic NO from its sum fails 8, perturbing one anthropogenic gas or aerosol flux by 1e-3 fails 8 and 16, feeding Bio the second layer's temperature fails 48, and moving one species' source to layer 2 fails 8. The emissions FORTRAN_BUGS findings (N116, B25) are reproduced by the components and therefore here: isoprene's tendency is identically zero although both E_ISO and the Gunther isoprene are nonzero.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "emissions",
      "chem_opt 170",
      "coupling"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte. Bound into the column grid at the import edge."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Bio": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/gunther_biogenic.esm"
    },
    "BioCbmz": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/gunther_to_cbmz.esm"
    },
    "Anthro": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/cbmz_anthropogenic.esm"
    },
    "Aer": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/mosaic_anthropogenic.esm"
    },
    "EmissionsColumn": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
