          "id": "chem170_emis_default_step1",
          "description": "Reference: the chem_opt = 170 emissions capture (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_emis.sh, MODE=default: emiss_opt = 4, emiss_inpt_opt = 1, bio_emiss_opt = 1; GNU gfortran real32 in model; fork ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, the `emissions` hook around emissions_driver in chem/chem_driver.F) at model step 1 (dt = 60 s), column (its, jts); USGS category 2, day 170, gsw 69.5174 W/m2. Inputs are the dumped column state and the dumped emission fields of layer 1. Expected values are the WHOLE emissions_driver increment over the step divided by dt, (chem_out - chem_in)/dt at every layer, from the real64 replay of bio_emissions, cbmz_addemiss_anthro, add_biogenics and mosaic_addemiss compiled unchanged and called in emissions_driver's order (kernels/emissions_driver), at 1e-9 of each column's maximum; so e_bio reaches add_biogenics through the coupling, not as an input. 58 of the 233 chem species change, all in layer 1, and every one of them is asserted here (the fill script refuses a case where a species changes that the document does not expose). The in-model real32 increments differ from the replay by at most 9e-05 relative.",
